# Model Card: LumenStay Booking Cancellation Risk Model

## Model

LightGBM binary classifier.

## Intended use

Prioritize booking-time retention support and inventory-management actions.

## Target

`cancelled_flag`: 1 if reservation cancels before arrival; 0 otherwise.

## Performance

| Metric | Untouched test result |
|---|---:|
| ROC-AUC | 0.7494 |
| Average precision | 0.3693 |
| Precision | 0.3360 |
| Recall | 0.6227 |
| F1 score | 0.4365 |

## High-risk threshold

Predicted cancellation probability >= 0.5582.

## Appropriate use

- Prioritize low-cost confirmation or modification options.
- Prioritize high-risk bookings for retention review.
- Support property × arrival-date expected-completed-stay forecasting.

## Inappropriate use

- Automatic booking denial.
- Automatic penalties.
- Broad incentives for every flagged booking.
- Treating feature importance as causal proof.

## Known limitations

- Predicts whether, not when, a cancellation may occur.
- Predictive associations are not causal.
- Performance may drift as properties, channels, pricing, or external-score methods change.
- Intervention effectiveness must be tested in randomized or phased pilots.

## Monitoring

Monitor monthly:

- ROC-AUC and average precision.
- Calibration by risk tier.
- Missingness and unseen-category rates.
- Cancellation rate by risk tier.
- Customer opt-outs, complaints, offer cost, and incremental completed stays.
